  "conclusion": [
    "r786 produced 15 decoded attack packets and diagnostic clip 30 to 29, but a valid post-attack frame still had no first-person arms or gun.",
    "All seven new sessions confirmed tag_origin to viewmodel_ak47 pointer write and readback, then restored the exact original pointer; valid captures still showed no arms/gun. Black frames were excluded.",
    "Disabling motion probe (r788), disabling read-only decoder (r789), restoring legacy nul ring mode (r792), binding early but observing after 1300 snapshots (r790), or binding late (r791) did not singly reproduce r755.",
    "The prior positive run had arms visible before binding, whereas current valid before-binding frames have no arms. The active first-person model list is the next data source to compare.",
    "No real firing or hit accepted; r787 had no decoded attack packets in the relevant late interval, so its left-click result cannot be interpreted as a shooting failure."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "This experiment has no current native DObj/model-list readout and does not identify the cause of missing arms.",
    "Memory pointer intervention is a reversible diagnostic and not a persistent service-side weapon registration fix.",
    "r786/r788 attack reception with no visible firing and r786 diagnostic ammo decrement do not satisfy shooting acceptance.",
    "Normal end/lobby and literal ui_state != 5 not tested."
  ],
